# =============================================================================
# Road Guard - build context for the Python worker image (context = repo root).
#
# This is an ALLOWLIST, not a denylist: the first line excludes everything and
# the `!` lines add back only what worker.py -> main.process_video_with_models
# actually needs.
#
# Why an allowlist. The repo root carries ~500 MB of things a container must
# never receive: yolo11x.pt (114 MB) and yolov8m.pt (52 MB) at the root,
# weights/clrernet_model_best_culane.pth (264 MB), models/v3_boxes_detector.pt
# (52 MB), plus UnLanedet/, datasets/, tests_videos/ and every run's
# validation_output/ + demo_out/. A denylist would have to name each of those,
# and would silently start shipping the next output directory someone adds.
# Docker does not read .gitignore, so none of that is excluded by default.
#
# `**` (not `*`) is required to exclude nested paths: `*` never matches a `/`,
# so a bare `*` would exclude the `weights` entry but still ship
# `weights/clrernet_model_best_culane.pth`. Last matching pattern wins.
#
# backend/ and frontend/ build from their own contexts and keep their own
# .dockerignore files; they are excluded here so the worker image does not
# carry a second copy of node_modules.
# =============================================================================

**

# --- entrypoint + pipeline modules imported by main.py -----------------------
!worker.py
# worker_common.py holds everything worker.py does that is not transport (model
# loading, bundle unpacking, violation records); worker_offline.py is the same
# worker with local folders instead of R2, handy for debugging inside the image.
!worker_common.py
!worker_offline.py
# lane_render.py draws the detected lane markings into the annotated video and the
# evidence clips; worker.py installs it at start-up. run_lanes.py is the lanes-only
# entry point (offline), useful for debugging inside the image.
!lane_render.py
!run_lanes.py
!main.py
!Constants.py
!cloud_env.py
!video_handler.py
!undistort.py

!Objects/**
!speed_estimation/**
!violations/**
!line_crossing/**
!lpr/**
# tools/ holds fetch_models.py plus ghost_mask / motion_filter /
# shoulder_violation, which main.py imports for the violation path.
!tools/**
# worker/entrypoint.sh is COPYed into the image (the Dockerfiles themselves are
# passed with -f and do not need to be in the context).
!worker/**

# --- dependency manifests ----------------------------------------------------
!requirements.txt
!requirements-worker.txt

# --- weights: ONLY the three small ones we commit ----------------------------
# Named individually. Their parent directories hold much larger checkpoints that
# must stay out of the image; the big auto-downloadable base weights arrive at
# run time in the models-cache volume (see tools/fetch_models.py).
!israeli_plates.pt
!weights/phase3_v3_yellowprotect.pt
!models/tire_yolo11n.pt

# --- re-exclude noise that lives inside the allowed directories ---------------
# These come last: a later pattern overrides the `!` lines above.
# Both forms are needed: `**/__pycache__/**` drops the .pyc files, and
# `**/__pycache__` drops the now-empty directory entry itself.
**/__pycache__
**/__pycache__/**
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.pytest_cache/**
# Per-module test suites and their fixtures are not needed at run time.
tools/violation_labels.json
**/tests/**
